  "chapter": 1,
  "title": "The Accusative Case",
  "subtitle": "Direct objects · -ṃ (singular) and -e (plural) endings · Building two-part sentences",
  "tags": [
    "New",
    "Cases",
    "Masc. -a nouns"
  ],
  "minutes": 12,
  "revision": {
    "title": "Quick Revision — Lesson I",
    "summaryHtml": "In Lesson I you learned the <strong>Nominative case</strong> — the subject of a sentence. Masculine nouns in <em>-a</em> take <strong>-o</strong> (singular) and <strong>-ā</strong> (plural). Verbs use <strong>-ti</strong> (sg.) and <strong>-nti</strong> (pl.).",
    "connectionHtml": "<strong>Connection:</strong> The Nominative marks <em>who does</em> the action. Now you'll learn the Accusative — which marks <em>what receives</em> the action. Together they form a complete sentence: Subject + Object + Verb.",
    "questions": [
      {
        "q": "What is the Nominative singular ending for masc. <em>-a</em> nouns?",
        "a": "<strong>-o</strong> (naro)"
      },
      {
        "q": "How do you say \"Farmers plough\" in Pāli?",
        "a": "<strong>Kassakā kasanti</strong>"
      },
      {
        "q": "What verb ending marks plural present tense?",
        "a": "<strong>-nti</strong>"
      }
    ]
  },
  "teach": [
    {
      "id": "grammar",
      "title": "The Accusative CaseDirect Object",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "level": 2,
          "eyebrow": "Grammar",
          "html": "The <em>Accusative</em> Case<br>Direct Object"
        },
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "html": "The Accusative case marks the <strong>direct object</strong> of a sentence — the person or thing that <em>receives</em> the action of the verb. It answers: <em>Whom?</em> or <em>What?</em>"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "html": "If the Nominative tells us <strong>who acts</strong>, the Accusative tells us <strong>what is acted upon</strong>. Together, they form the basic Pāli sentence: Subject (Nom.) + Object (Acc.) + Verb."
        },
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "html": "The Accusative is also used for the <strong>goal of motion</strong> — the place someone is going <em>to</em>. For example: <em>Naro gāmaṃ gacchati</em> — \"The man goes to the village.\""
        },
        {
          "type": "rule",
          "title": "For masculine nouns ending in -a, the Accusative case endings are:",
          "formulas": [
            "Singular: base + <em>-ṃ</em> <span>|</span> nara + ṃ = <em>naraṃ</em>",
            "Plural:&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;base + <em>-e</em> <span>|</span> nara + e = <em>nare</em>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "caption": "Accusative declension of masculine -a nouns",
          "head": [
            "Case",
            "Base",
            "Ending",
            "Form",
            "Meaning"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Acc. singular",
              "<span class=\"decl-highlight\">nara</span>",
              "<span class=\"decl-ending\">+ ṃ</span>",
              "<span class=\"decl-highlight\"><span class=\"decl-base\">nara</span><span class=\"decl-ending\">ṃ</span></span>",
              "the man <em>(object)</em>"
            ],
            [
              "Acc. singular",
              "<span class=\"decl-highlight\">kassaka</span>",
              "<span class=\"decl-ending\">+ ṃ</span>",
              "<span class=\"decl-highlight\"><span class=\"decl-base\">kassaka</span><span class=\"decl-ending\">ṃ</span></span>",
              "the farmer"
            ],
            [
              "Acc. plural",
              "<span class=\"decl-highlight\">nara</span>",
              "<span class=\"decl-ending\">+ e</span>",
              "<span class=\"decl-highlight\"><span class=\"decl-base\">nar</span><span class=\"decl-ending\">e</span></span>",
              "men <em>(object)</em>"
            ],
            [
              "Acc. plural",
              "<span class=\"decl-highlight\">kassaka</span>",
              "<span class=\"decl-ending\">+ e</span>",
              "<span class=\"decl-highlight\"><span class=\"decl-base\">kassak</span><span class=\"decl-ending\">e</span></span>",
              "farmers"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
